Package: jlib
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: C++ cornucopia
 C++ libraries for crypto, net, media, gl, sys

Package: jhttpd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: static web server built on jlib
 An HTTP/1.1 server for static files: virtual hosts by name, TLS with SNI,
 basic authentication, rate limiting and a per-address connection cap, all
 from one nginx-shaped configuration file.
 .
 Ships a systemd unit and a logrotate snippet. The unit checks the
 configuration with "jhttpd --test" before replacing a running server, so a
 typo fails the start rather than the site.

Package: jlib-gl
Architecture: any
Depends: jlib (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: the graphical and audio half of jlib
 The jlib libraries and programs that link OpenGL, GLFW, X11 or portaudio,
 and the runtime dependencies that come with them.
 .
 Separate from jlib so that a headless machine -- a web server running
 jhttpd, say -- does not acquire an X11 stack in order to install a
 library it uses for sockets and strings.

Package: jlib-doc
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: architecture documentation for jlib
 The maps that the headers cannot be: how the reactor, the coroutine layer and
 the two server modes fit together, and what a request traverses end to end.
 Each document spans several files, which is why none of it lives at any one
 declaration.
 .
 Per-symbol documentation is in the headers, where it stays correct.
